---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@lib/site';

const lastUpdated = 'May 2025';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms that govern your use of Ember & Ink — content, comments, affiliate links, and liability."
  url={`${SITE.url}/terms/`}
>
  <article class="container-ember py-16 md:py-24 max-w-3xl">
    <header>
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted">
        The legal bits
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl md:text-5xl text-burgundy">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-ember mt-10">
      <p>
        By accessing {SITE.url}, you agree to these terms. If you do not
        agree, please do not use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Content</h2>
      <p>
        All written content, images, and design on Ember &amp; Ink are
        owned by Ember &amp; Ink or used with permission, unless otherwise
        stated. You may quote short excerpts with a clear link back to the
        original post. You may not republish full reviews or reuse cover
        images without written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Opinions</h2>
      <p>
        Reviews reflect the personal opinion of the writer at the time of
        writing. Books, tastes, and writers change. We make no claim that
        our opinion is universal or that a book we love will work for you.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Ember &amp; Ink participates in the Amazon Services LLC Associates
        Program and may include affiliate links. See the
        <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> for full
        details. Affiliate income never influences editorial opinion.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        The site links to third-party sites (Amazon, publishers, other
        blogs). We do not control those sites and are not responsible for
        their content or practices.
      </p>

      <h2>5. No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided "as is". We make no guarantees about
        availability, accuracy, or fitness for a particular purpose. If a
        book we recommend doesn't land for you, we're sorry — but we can't
        offer a refund.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, Ember &amp; Ink is not
        liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential loss
        arising from your use of the site or reliance on its content.
      </p>

      <h2>7. User submissions</h2>
      <p>
        If you send us a message, review request, or testimonial, you grant
        us permission to reply to you and (for testimonials shared with
        explicit consent) to feature your words on the site with
        attribution. We will never sell or share your contact details.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. Continued use of the
        site after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
        or use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>